"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs=self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs||[]).push([[909],{59321(e,r,o){e.exports=o.p+"assets/img/seller-restriction.d58ef75c.webp"},87566(e,r,o){o.r(r),o.d(r,{comp:()=>v,data:()=>y});var t=o(20641);const s=o.p+"assets/img/seller-store-edit-overview.fd9a5d39.png",n=o.p+"assets/img/seller-store-edit-images-card.15666642.png",i=o.p+"assets/img/seller-store-edit-store-hours-card.1971bfbe.png",a=o.p+"assets/img/seller-store-edit-kyc-card.ce78e131.png",l=o.p+"assets/img/seller-store-edit-profile-view-card.4017215c.png",d=o.p+"assets/img/seller-store-edit-seo-card.f64f1b17.png",c=o.p+"assets/img/seller-store-edit-general-card.40871c8b.png",g=o.p+"assets/img/seller-store-edit-social-card.d7afd56d.png",p=o.p+"assets/img/seller-store-edit-shop-info-card.49157ce5.png";var h=o(59321);const u=o.p+"assets/img/seller-public-storefront-view.1eb4c868.png",m={class:"hint-container tip"},f={},v=(0,o(66262).A)(f,[["render",function(e,r){const o=(0,t.g2)("RouteLink");return(0,t.uX)(),(0,t.CE)("div",null,[r[8]||(r[8]=(0,t.Fv)('<h1 id="vendor-profile" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#vendor-profile"><span>Vendor Profile</span></a></h1><p>The <strong>Vendor Profile</strong> displays essential information about a vendor&#39;s shop, helping buyers learn about the store, view products, review store policies, and verify vendor credibility.</p><p>In the modern seller dashboard, vendor profile management is handled on the <strong>Store Edit</strong> page (<code>/seller/vendor-profile/</code>). Unlike older tab-based layouts, the new setup organizes all profile configurations into a <strong>single, scrollable two-column card layout</strong>. Vendors can view and manage their entire store configuration in one unified workspace without clicking between tabs.</p>',3)),(0,t.Lk)("div",m,[r[7]||(r[7]=(0,t.Lk)("p",{class:"hint-container-title"},"Using the classic layout?",-1)),(0,t.Lk)("p",null,[r[1]||(r[1]=(0,t.eW)("If your marketplace uses the older ")),r[2]||(r[2]=(0,t.Lk)("strong",null,"My Account",-1)),r[3]||(r[3]=(0,t.eW)(" tabbed layout (")),r[4]||(r[4]=(0,t.Lk)("strong",null,"My Account → My Profile",-1)),r[5]||(r[5]=(0,t.eW)("), please refer to the ")),(0,t.bF)(o,{to:"/documentation/classic-vendor-profile.html"},{default:(0,t.k6)(()=>r[0]||(r[0]=[(0,t.eW)("Classic Vendor Profile")])),_:1}),r[6]||(r[6]=(0,t.eW)(" guide. You can switch between layouts using the dashboard view options configured by the marketplace administrator."))])]),r[9]||(r[9]=(0,t.Fv)('<hr><h2 id="store-edit-layout-overview" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#store-edit-layout-overview"><span>Store Edit Layout Overview</span></a></h2><p>Vendors can access their profile editor directly from the seller dashboard sidebar by clicking <strong>Store Edit</strong> (<code>/seller/vendor-profile/</code>).</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/seller-store-edit-overview.png"><img src="'+s+'" alt="Store Edit Page Overview"></a></p><hr><h2 id="main-column-cards" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#main-column-cards"><span>Main Column Cards</span></a></h2><p>The main column contains the core store configurations, media assets, business hours, compliance verification, storefront layout selection, and search engine optimization.</p><hr><h3 id="_1-images-card" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-images-card"><span>1. Images Card</span></a></h3><p>The <strong>Images</strong> card manages the visual branding of the vendor&#39;s store across both the seller dashboard and customer-facing pages.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/seller-store-edit-images-card.png"><img src="'+n+'" alt="Store Edit Images Card"></a></p><ul><li><strong>Allowed File Formats</strong>: Supports <code>jpg</code>, <code>jpeg</code>, <code>png</code>, <code>webp</code>, and <code>gif</code>.</li><li><strong>User Image</strong>: The personal profile avatar of the vendor. Includes <strong>Upload</strong> and <strong>Remove</strong> buttons with instant image preview.</li><li><strong>Shop Logo</strong>: The official brand logo for the store, visible on the vendor&#39;s storefront, product pages, and invoice headers.</li><li><strong>Panel Header</strong>: A dropdown setting that configures the branding area in the top-left corner of the seller dashboard: <ul><li><strong>Logo with shop name</strong>: Displays both the store logo and the store name together.</li><li><strong>Logo only</strong>: Displays only the logo image in the top-left navigation panel.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Banner Image</strong>: A wide header banner displayed across the top of the vendor&#39;s public store page. <ul><li><strong>Show banner on vendor page</strong>: Checkbox toggle to show or hide the banner on the public storefront.</li><li>Includes <strong>Upload</strong> and <strong>Remove</strong> controls to update or clear the banner image anytime.</li></ul></li></ul><hr><h3 id="_2-shop-configuration-card" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-shop-configuration-card"><span>2. Shop Configuration Card</span></a></h3><p>The <strong>Shop</strong> card contains store contact details, payout preferences, analytics tracking, tax compliance, geographical location, and public store policies.</p><h4 id="store-information-payouts" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#store-information-payouts"><span>Store Information &amp; Payouts:</span></a></h4><ul><li><strong>Shop Name</strong>: The public display name of the store.</li><li><strong>Shop Slug</strong>: The URL slug representing the store (for example, <code>/vendor/aurora-athletics</code>). This field is read-only after initial creation to protect permanent store links and SEO indexing.</li><li><strong>Phone Number</strong>: Customer service or store contact telephone number (accepts 4 to 15 characters).</li><li><strong>Payment Information</strong>: Vendor payout details (such as direct bank account numbers, SWIFT/IBAN codes, or PayPal address) used by the admin to disburse earnings after deducting commission.</li></ul><h4 id="google-analytics-tracking" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#google-analytics-tracking"><span>Google Analytics Tracking:</span></a></h4><p>Vendors can track customer traffic and engagement on their own store pages:</p><ul><li><strong>Google Analytics Account ID</strong>: Enter your Google Analytics Measurement ID (e.g., <code>G-XXXXXXXXXX</code>).</li><li><strong>Enable Tracking Events</strong>: <ul><li><strong>Enable view item event</strong>: Fires when a customer views any product belonging to the vendor.</li><li><strong>Enable purchase event</strong>: Fires when a customer completes an order containing the vendor&#39;s products.</li></ul></li></ul><h4 id="tax-system-compliance" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#tax-system-compliance"><span>Tax System Compliance:</span></a></h4><ul><li><strong>Choose Tax System</strong>: Select the applicable tax registration authority from the dropdown: <ul><li><strong>GSTIN</strong> (Goods and Services Tax Identification Number)</li><li><strong>SSN</strong> (Social Security Number)</li><li><strong>VAT</strong> (Value Added Tax)</li></ul></li><li><strong>Tax Identification Number</strong>: Input field corresponding to the selected tax system (e.g., GSTIN number, VAT registration, or SSN). This ID is displayed on store receipts and verified by the marketplace.</li></ul><h4 id="store-address-interactive-location-map" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#store-address-interactive-location-map"><span>Store Address &amp; Interactive Location Map:</span></a></h4><ul><li><strong>Country</strong>: Dropdown list to choose the country of operation.</li><li><strong>Shop Address</strong>: Street address and office/building number.</li><li><strong>Interactive Map</strong>: Vendors can search their location or drag the map pin to mark their physical shop.</li><li><strong>Shop Latitude &amp; Longitude</strong>: Automatically populated by the map pin, ensuring the store appears accurately on marketplace store locator maps.</li><li><strong>City, State, and Postal Code</strong>: Specific regional address details.</li></ul><h4 id="store-policies-bio" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#store-policies-bio"><span>Store Policies &amp; Bio:</span></a></h4><p>Each policy section includes a rich-text / WYSIWYG editor allowing text formatting, links, and bullet points:</p><ul><li><strong>About Shop</strong>: A detailed description of the store, brand story, craftsmanship, or specialty shown in the &quot;About this Vendor&quot; section on the storefront.</li><li><strong>Return Policy</strong>: Guidelines and timelines for product returns, warranty claims, and refunds.</li><li><strong>Shipping Policy</strong>: Information on handling times, domestic/international carriers, and delivery expectations.</li><li><strong>Privacy Policy</strong>: How customer personal data is handled and protected by the vendor.</li></ul><hr><h3 id="_3-store-hours-card" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-store-hours-card"><span>3. Store Hours Card</span></a></h3><p>The <strong>Store Hours</strong> card allows vendors to define their weekly operating schedule and control whether buyers can purchase products outside business hours.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/seller-store-edit-store-hours-card.png"><img src="'+i+'" alt="Store Edit Store Hours Card"></a></p><h4 id="general-store-hours-controls" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#general-store-hours-controls"><span>General Store Hours Controls:</span></a></h4><ul><li><strong>Enable Store Hours</strong>: Switch toggle to turn the store schedule on or off. When active, opening hours appear on the vendor&#39;s store page.</li><li><strong>Disable Purchase During OFF Time</strong>: Switch toggle to block the &quot;Add to Cart&quot; button on the vendor&#39;s products whenever the store is closed.</li><li><strong>Store Off Time Message</strong>: A customizable notice displayed to shoppers on store and product pages when the shop is closed (e.g., <em>&quot;Our workshop is currently closed. Orders placed outside operating hours will be processed the next business morning.&quot;</em>). Basic HTML formatting is supported.</li></ul><h4 id="weekly-schedule" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#weekly-schedule"><span>Weekly Schedule:</span></a></h4><ul><li>Each day from <strong>Monday to Sunday</strong> has an independent <strong>Open / Closed</strong> toggle.</li><li>For open days, vendors can define operating time slots (<strong>Start Time</strong> and <strong>End Time</strong>).</li><li>Vendors can click <strong>+ Add Slot</strong> to set split shifts or multiple open intervals within the same day (such as morning and evening hours).</li></ul><hr><h3 id="_4-kyc-verification-card" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-kyc-verification-card"><span>4. KYC Verification Card</span></a></h3><p>The <strong>KYC</strong> (Know Your Customer) card provides identity and compliance verification with the marketplace administration.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/seller-store-edit-kyc-card.png"><img src="'+a+'" alt="Store Edit KYC Verification Card"></a></p><ul><li><strong>Verification Status Badge</strong>: Displays the current verification state of the vendor&#39;s documents: <ul><li><strong>Not uploaded</strong>: No documents have been submitted yet.</li><li><strong>Pending</strong>: Document is uploaded and awaiting administrator review.</li><li><strong>Approved</strong>: Document is verified by the admin.</li><li><strong>Rejected</strong>: Document was not accepted (the vendor must re-upload a valid file).</li></ul></li><li><strong>KYC Document Type</strong>: Dropdown selection specifying the type of submitted proof: <ul><li><strong>Business License</strong></li><li><strong>Government ID</strong></li><li><strong>Utility Bill</strong></li></ul></li><li><strong>KYC Document File</strong>: File upload input. Supported document formats include <code>pdf</code>, <code>jpg</code>, <code>jpeg</code>, and <code>png</code>.</li></ul><hr><h3 id="_5-profile-view-card" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-profile-view-card"><span>5. Profile View Card</span></a></h3><p>The <strong>Profile View</strong> card lets vendors customize how their public storefront is styled and laid out for shoppers, with an embedded <strong>Live Preview</strong>.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/seller-store-edit-profile-view-card.png"><img src="'+l+'" alt="Store Edit Profile View Card"></a></p><h4 id="storefront-layout-options" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#storefront-layout-options"><span>Storefront Layout Options:</span></a></h4><ul><li><strong>Storefront</strong>: A clean, structured store layout featuring a dedicated information sidebar displaying store hours, contact details, map location, and a grid product gallery.</li><li><strong>Spotlight</strong>: A visually driven layout with a full-width hero banner, prominent product showcases front and center, and an expanded &quot;About this Vendor&quot; story section.</li></ul><h4 id="live-preview" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#live-preview"><span>Live Preview:</span></a></h4><ul><li>Directly underneath the options, an embedded <strong>Live Preview frame</strong> loads the vendor&#39;s store page in real time. Switching between <strong>Storefront</strong> and <strong>Spotlight</strong> instantly updates the live frame so vendors can verify their design before saving.</li></ul><hr><h3 id="_6-seo-information-card" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_6-seo-information-card"><span>6. SEO Information Card</span></a></h3><p>The <strong>SEO Information</strong> card optimizes how the vendor&#39;s shop appears on search engines (like Google, Bing) and AI search summaries.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/seller-store-edit-seo-card.png"><img src="'+d+'" alt="Store Edit SEO Information Card"></a></p><ul><li><strong>Live Search Snippet Preview</strong>: A real-time Google search result preview box showing the page title, clean store URL (<code>/vendor/[slug]</code>), and meta description as searchers will see it in search engine result pages (SERPs).</li><li><strong>Meta Title</strong>: The title tag shown in search engine results and browser tabs. Recommended length is 50–60 characters.</li><li><strong>Meta Keywords</strong>: Keywords describing the vendor&#39;s store, categories, and specialty products. Multiple keywords must be separated by commas (e.g., <code>running shoes, trail footwear, sports apparel</code>).</li><li><strong>Meta Description</strong>: A concise summary of the store and offerings (recommended 150–160 characters). A well-crafted description improves click-through rates from search results.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="sidebar-column-cards" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#sidebar-column-cards"><span>Sidebar Column Cards</span></a></h2><p>The right column of the Store Edit page displays personal vendor details, connected social media channels, and administrative permissions.</p><hr><h3 id="_7-general-card" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_7-general-card"><span>7. General Card</span></a></h3><p>The <strong>General</strong> card contains basic personal profile details for the vendor account.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/seller-store-edit-general-card.png"><img src="'+c+'" alt="Store Edit General Details Card"></a></p><ul><li><strong>Username</strong>: The account login handle (read-only; set during initial registration).</li><li><strong>First Name</strong>: The vendor&#39;s first name.</li><li><strong>Last Name</strong>: The vendor&#39;s last name.</li><li><strong>E-Mail</strong>: The primary email address for notifications, order alerts, and account communications.</li></ul><hr><h3 id="_8-social-profile-card" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-social-profile-card"><span>8. Social Profile Card</span></a></h3><p>The <strong>Social Profile</strong> card connects the vendor&#39;s external social media presences to their marketplace store page.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/seller-store-edit-social-card.png"><img src="'+g+'" alt="Store Edit Social Profile Card"></a></p><p>Vendors can enter full profile URLs (<code>https://...</code>) for the following platforms:</p><ul><li><strong>Facebook Profile ID</strong></li><li><strong>Instagram Profile ID</strong></li><li><strong>X (Formerly Twitter) Profile ID</strong></li><li><strong>Linkedin Profile ID</strong></li><li><strong>Youtube Profile</strong></li><li><strong>Pinterest Profile</strong></li></ul><p>Connected profiles appear as clickable social media icons on the public vendor storefront.</p><hr><h3 id="_9-shop-information-card-read-only-admin-settings" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_9-shop-information-card-read-only-admin-settings"><span>9. Shop Information Card (Read-Only Admin Settings)</span></a></h3><p>The <strong>Shop Information</strong> card provides a clear, read-only summary of the marketplace permissions, commission rate, and capabilities assigned to the vendor by the administrator.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/seller-store-edit-shop-info-card.png"><img src="'+p+'" alt="Store Edit Shop Information Card"></a></p><ul><li><strong>Applied Commission</strong>: The current commission percentage deducted by the marketplace on the vendor&#39;s sales (e.g., <code>12%</code>). If no vendor-specific rate is set, the global marketplace rate applies.</li><li><strong>Allowed Categories</strong>: Tags/chips showing which product categories the vendor is authorized to list products under (e.g., <em>Sports &amp; Outdoors</em>, <em>Clothing</em>, <em>Accessories</em>).</li><li><strong>Allowed Product Types</strong>: Tags/chips listing permitted product types (e.g., <em>Simple product</em>, <em>Grouped product</em>, <em>External/Affiliate product</em>, <em>Variable product</em>).</li><li><strong>Payment Methods</strong>: Payout channels enabled by the admin for disbursing seller earnings (e.g., <em>Direct bank transfer</em>, <em>Check payments</em>, <em>Cash on delivery</em>).</li><li><strong>Shipping Methods</strong>: Shipping carriers and delivery options permitted for the vendor (e.g., <em>Flat rate</em>, <em>Free shipping</em>, <em>Store Pickup</em>).</li></ul><div class="hint-container note"><p class="hint-container-title">Read-Only Permissions</p><p>The settings in the Shop Information card are configured by the marketplace admin. If you need additional categories, product types, or custom commission rates, contact the marketplace administrator.</p></div><hr><h2 id="saving-profile-changes" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#saving-profile-changes"><span>Saving Profile Changes</span></a></h2><p>Once you have updated your store information across any of the cards:</p><ol><li>Review the entered details and live previews.</li><li>Click the <strong>Save</strong> button located at the <strong>top-right</strong> corner of the Store Edit page.</li><li>A success confirmation notice confirms that all updated fields have been saved.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="vendor-purchase-restriction" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#vendor-purchase-restriction"><span>Vendor Purchase Restriction</span></a></h2><p>To ensure marketplace trust, prevent fraudulent transactions, and comply with review integrity:</p><ul><li>Vendors are <strong>restricted from purchasing their own products</strong>.</li><li>If a logged-in vendor views one of their own products on the storefront, the standard &quot;Add to Cart&quot; button is disabled or replaced with an <strong>Edit Product</strong> link.</li><li>The <strong>Edit Product</strong> shortcut allows vendors to quickly jump straight from the customer storefront into the seller catalog editor.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/seller-restriction.webp"><img src="'+h+'" alt="Vendor Purchase Restriction"></a></p><hr><h2 id="vendor-profile-–-frontend-view" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#vendor-profile-–-frontend-view"><span>Vendor Profile – Frontend View</span></a></h2><p>When shoppers visit a vendor&#39;s public store link (<code>/vendor/[shop-slug]</code>), they see the fully branded storefront based on the chosen profile layout (<strong>Storefront</strong> or <strong>Spotlight</strong>):</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/seller-public-storefront-view.png"><img src="'+u+'" alt="Public Vendor Storefront View"></a></p><h3 id="public-storefront-elements" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#public-storefront-elements"><span>Public Storefront Elements:</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Store Banner &amp; Logo</strong>: Branded header imagery and store logo.</li><li><strong>Vendor Badges</strong>: Verified maker, on-time delivery, and excellence badges assigned by the administrator.</li><li><strong>Deals in Categories</strong>: Interactive category badges highlighting product lines offered by the store.</li><li><strong>Store Location &amp; Hours</strong>: Physical street address, interactive map, and real-time open/closed status.</li><li><strong>About this Vendor</strong>: Store biography and brand story.</li><li><strong>Store Policies</strong>: Dedicated tabs displaying the vendor&#39;s Return Policy, Shipping Policy, and Privacy Policy.</li><li><strong>Product Catalog</strong>: Paginated grid of all published products with search, sorting, and price filtering.</li><li><strong>Customer Reviews &amp; Inquiry</strong>: Review submission form, average customer rating, and &quot;Ask a Question&quot; / &quot;Report Vendor&quot; links.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="frequently-asked-questions-faq" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#frequently-asked-questions-faq"><span>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</span></a></h2><details><summary><strong>Can I change my Shop Slug after setting up my store?</strong></summary><p>In the Store Edit interface, the <strong>Shop Slug</strong> field is read-only after creation. This protects your store URL (<code>/vendor/[slug]</code>), prevents broken backlinks, and maintains search engine rankings. If you need an exceptional change to your store slug, request a slug update from the marketplace administrator.</p></details><details><summary><strong>Where do I find my applied commission rate?</strong></summary><p>Your current commission rate is displayed in the <strong>Shop Information</strong> card in the right sidebar column of the Store Edit page. This rate is set by the marketplace administrator.</p></details><details><summary><strong>What happens to my products when Store Hours are closed?</strong></summary><p>If the <strong>Disable Purchase During OFF Time</strong> toggle is enabled, customers cannot add your items to their cart while your store is closed. A friendly off-time notice (configured in your <strong>Store Off Time Message</strong> field) is displayed on your store and product pages.</p></details><details><summary><strong>What file formats are accepted for Images and KYC documents?</strong></summary><ul><li><strong>Store Images</strong> (User avatar, Shop logo, Banner): <code>jpg</code>, <code>jpeg</code>, <code>png</code>, <code>webp</code>, and <code>gif</code>.</li><li><strong>KYC Verification Documents</strong>: <code>pdf</code>, <code>jpg</code>, <code>jpeg</code>, and <code>png</code>.</li></ul></details><details><summary><strong>Do I need to save each section individually?</strong></summary><p>No. The new Store Edit layout features a unified <strong>Save</strong> button in the top-right corner of the page. Clicking this button saves changes across all cards at once.</p></details>',96))])}]]),y=JSON.parse('{"path":"/documentation/vendor-profile.html","title":"Vendor Profile","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{},"headers":[{"level":2,"title":"Store Edit Layout Overview","slug":"store-edit-layout-overview","link":"#store-edit-layout-overview","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Main Column Cards","slug":"main-column-cards","link":"#main-column-cards","children":[{"level":3,"title":"1. Images Card","slug":"_1-images-card","link":"#_1-images-card","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"2. Shop Configuration Card","slug":"_2-shop-configuration-card","link":"#_2-shop-configuration-card","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"3. Store Hours Card","slug":"_3-store-hours-card","link":"#_3-store-hours-card","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"4. KYC Verification Card","slug":"_4-kyc-verification-card","link":"#_4-kyc-verification-card","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"5. Profile View Card","slug":"_5-profile-view-card","link":"#_5-profile-view-card","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"6. SEO Information Card","slug":"_6-seo-information-card","link":"#_6-seo-information-card","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Sidebar Column Cards","slug":"sidebar-column-cards","link":"#sidebar-column-cards","children":[{"level":3,"title":"7. General Card","slug":"_7-general-card","link":"#_7-general-card","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"8. Social Profile Card","slug":"_8-social-profile-card","link":"#_8-social-profile-card","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"9. Shop Information Card (Read-Only Admin Settings)","slug":"_9-shop-information-card-read-only-admin-settings","link":"#_9-shop-information-card-read-only-admin-settings","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Saving Profile Changes","slug":"saving-profile-changes","link":"#saving-profile-changes","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Vendor Purchase Restriction","slug":"vendor-purchase-restriction","link":"#vendor-purchase-restriction","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Vendor Profile – Frontend View","slug":"vendor-profile-–-frontend-view","link":"#vendor-profile-–-frontend-view","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Public Storefront Elements:","slug":"public-storefront-elements","link":"#public-storefront-elements","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)","slug":"frequently-asked-questions-faq","link":"#frequently-asked-questions-faq","children":[]}],"git":{},"filePathRelative":"documentation/vendor-profile.md"}')}}]);